+### CoroNeRF
+A differentiable multiline neural tomography framework for the direct joint recovery of 3D electron density and temperature from multiview spectral line-intensity images [S8, unofficial]. For each ray $q$ parameterized as $x_q(t) = o_q + t d_q$ for $t \in [t_s(q), t_f(q)]$, it evaluates channel-dependent emissivity $\epsilon_c(n_e, T_e, r)$ using a precomputed atomic-physics lookup table (CHIANTI database) at samples along the ray [S8, unofficial]. It optimizes neural plasma field parameters $\theta$ by minimizing the image loss over the training ray dataset $D_{ray}$: $\theta^* = \arg\min_\theta \frac{1}{|D_{ray}|} \sum_{(x_q(\cdot), y_q) \in D_{ray}} \frac{1}{C} \sum_{c=1}^C \rho(\hat{I}_{\theta,q,c}, y_{q,c})$ [S8, unofficial]. The asinh-L1 image loss yields lower field error than the inverse-variance-weighted squared-residual objective, despite images having heteroscedastic Gaussian noise [S8, unofficial].
+
+### DLR-NeRF Training Schedule
+Phase b: Fine-tune LR-NeRF with the same configuration as Phase a, but camera pose parameters are no longer updated. Train for $3 \times 10^5$ iterations. Set ADMM penalty factor $\rho = 10$ [S9, unofficial]. Phase c: After TT decomposition and initialization of DLR-NeRF, fine-tune DLR-NeRF for $2 \times 10^5$ iterations with camera pose parameters fixed [S9, unofficial]. Phase d: Quantize DLR-NeRF layers gradually from first to last. After quantizing each layer, train the other layers for $3 \times 10^4$ iterations. Initialize the codebook for interval $[-1, 1]$ using k-means clustering for 20 iterations [S9, unofficial]. Hardware: GeForce RTX 2080 Ti with 11 GB memory. Framework: PyTorch [S9, unofficial].
+
+### A-NeRF Baseline Configuration
+Use a bigger foreground mask for ray sampling. Enable background estimation in the official code. Use L2 loss instead of L1 loss [S10]. A-NeRF uses only keypoints instead of surface models to construct conditional inputs to NeRF networks, making it easy to confuse background and foreground, resulting in floating blob artifacts [S10]. A-NeRF cannot generalize to unseen poses when training poses are limited, yielding the worst generalization results among baselines on ZJU-MoCap [S10].
 
